# K2: the TIMED arm. c2-packed-tp4-speed is the gate profile with the verify's T1 shard-argmax and T2 window audits OFF
# (QWEN_FAST_VERIFY_T1_AUDIT=0, QWEN_FAST_VERIFY_T2_AUDIT=0) and the drafter's K/V slide ON. The same four tests as K1. The round
# time, the single-user coding decode rate and the concurrent4 per-user rates are read from THIS arm. The S2 window's v140 (audits
# on, eager ramp publication) measured 4-live rounds of 814 ms (5.1 tok/s per user) and single-user coding of 35.7 tok/s.
# Projection to confirm or refute: a 4-live round of about 175 ms (readback 31 ms less, ramp commits about 5 ms instead of about 310
# ms each) at v140's two-ramp / two-steady mix, and about 155 ms with four steady users.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 5-15 min (the kernels are cached by K1); tests 8-15 min: 15 / 25 / 60 min.
# Read: [PACKED-PHASE] (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] (kv, proj) per round,
# medians at 4 live; readback_ms (expect about 2 ms, not 33-55); the coding decode_tok_s; the concurrent4 per-user decode_tok_s and
# the [ACCEPT] mean; the warm_lifecycle TTFT.
# The warm_lifecycle runs before coding, so the coding TTFT here is WARM: it cannot be compared with v140's cold 19.46 s (no job
# of this window measures cold 8k TTFT, and nothing on tp4/speed changes TTFT: do not report a better TTFT here as a fix).
# STOP on a hang or garbage text (c2_smoke_check.py enforces both); otherwise the numbers are the product.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,warm_lifecycle,coding,concurrent4
